===Verb===
{{en-verb|pres_ptc2=parasolling|past2=parasolled}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To protect with, or as if with, a parasol; to [[shade]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1826|title=The Monthly Magazine|page=161
|passage=Now old ladies, who dare venture a-shopping, go '''parasolling''' their withered perfections along, and entertain a decided dread of injuring the immaterial whiteness of their skins, which have ceased to he compared to "lilies" and "snows," and other sonnet-like similes, for more than thirty summers {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Geoff Ryman|title=The King's Last Song|page=19
|passage={{...}} the buffaloes in the mire, and rows of trees '''parasolling''' houses along the waterways.}}

